@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "How to play";
}
<div class="mx-auto" style="max-width: 42rem">
    <h1 class="h2 mb-4">How to play</h1>
    <ol class="ao-rules">
        <li><strong>Start a challenge.</strong> Pick <strong>Easy</strong> (about 40 arrows), <strong>Medium</strong> (about 200) or <strong>Hard</strong> (400–700). Every challenge is a brand-new random labyrinth of mostly long paths that twist and turn, packed side by side.</li>
        <li><strong>Tap an arrow.</strong> It slides along its own path in the direction its head points until it leaves the board.</li>
        <li><strong>Watch the path.</strong> If another arrow sits anywhere ahead of the head, the arrow bumps into it, bounces back and you lose a heart.</li>
        <li><strong>Clear the board.</strong> Remove every arrow to win. Fewer collisions earn more stars.</li>
        <li><strong>Zoom in.</strong> Scroll or pinch to zoom, drag to move around the board, or use the <i class="bi bi-zoom-in"></i> <i class="bi bi-zoom-out"></i> buttons.</li>
        <li><strong>Stuck?</strong> Use a hint (three per attempt) to highlight an arrow that can safely leave.</li>
        <li><strong>Points.</strong> Every board you clear earns points for the leaderboard: <strong>Easy 1</strong>, <strong>Medium 4</strong>, <strong>Hard 10</strong>. Each board scores once — replaying a board you already won earns nothing extra.</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="text-muted">Keyboard: <kbd>H</kbd> asks for a hint, <kbd>R</kbd> restarts, <kbd>+</kbd> / <kbd>-</kbd> zoom, <kbd>0</kbd> shows the whole board and <kbd>G</kbd> toggles the grid.</p>
    <a class="btn btn-ao" asp-controller="Home" asp-action="Index"><i class="bi bi-play-fill me-1"></i>Play</a>
</div>
